m>(penget \/ megr\u00e1nt)<\/em><\/p><p>Farmers often _______ weeds from their fields to ensure a healthy crop. <em>(gyoml\u00e1l \/ kih\u00faz)<\/em><\/p><p>With a sudden _______, he pulled the thorn from his finger. <em>(r\u00e1nt\u00e1s \/ h\u00faz\u00e1s)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 197, 94);\">t\u00e9p \/ leszak\u00edt \/ penget \/ b\u00e1tors\u00e1g<\/span><\/p><p><span>Negative meaning (HU): gy\u00e1vas\u00e1g \/ f\u00e9lelem \/ megfutamod\u00e1s<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ up the courage = \u00f6sszeszedi a b\u00e1tors\u00e1g\u00e1t (pl. He had to _______ up the courage to speak in public.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a string = megpenget egy h\u00fart (pl. She gently _______ed a string on her harp.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a feather = kit\u00e9p egy tollat (pl. The bird began to _______ a feather from its wing.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a flower = leszak\u00edt egy vir\u00e1got (pl. He went to the garden to _______ a flower for his mother.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>pluck<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>pluck<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>pluck<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: pluck up \/ pluck a string \/ pluck a feather \/ pluck a flower<\/span><\/p><p>similar: pull \/ pick \/ courage \/ bravery<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: cowardice \/ fear \/ timidity<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":1,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-13T18:42:22+00:00"},{"id":51282,"front":"<p>He decided to _______ down and rest for a while. <em>(pihen \/ nyugszik)<\/em><\/p><p>The company was accused of deliberately _______ the truth about its financial situation. <em>(elhallgat \/ elferd\u00edt